["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalRefType/productMetadata", "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition", "A reference to additional product metadata such as a reference within an organization's product catalog.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Software/Sbom", "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note", "A Software Bill of Materials (SBOM) is a collection of SPDX Elements describing\na single package.\n\nThis could include details of the content and composition of the product,\nprovenance details of the product and/or its composition, licensing\ninformation, known quality or security issues, etc.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["_:N8cc50242ea724dd4bd46f932bdc2c1d6", "http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#path", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/version", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/ExpandedLicensing/ListedLicense", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/ExpandedLicensing/License", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/RelationshipType/createdBy", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "The from Action or DefinedProcess is createdBy to Agent(s).", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Software/Package", "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note", "A package refers to any unit of content that can be associated with a\ndistribution of software.\n\nTypically, a package is composed of one or more files.\n\nAny of the following non-limiting examples may be (but are not required to be)\nrepresented in SPDX as a package:\n\n- a tarball, zip file or other archive\n- a directory or sub-directory\n- a separately distributed piece of software which another Package or File uses\n  or depends upon (e.g., a Python package, a Go module, ...)\n- a container image, and/or each image layer within a container image\n- a collection of one or more sub-packages\n- a Git repository snapshot from a particular point in time\n\nNote that some of these could be represented in SPDX as a file as well.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalRefType/runtimeAnalysisReport", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label", "runtimeAnalysisReport", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["_:Nc0eaf2f65ae34da3bc0e551594444ef2", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first", "_:Nbfbf727d924a498fbfd092a2ebddaeac", "localId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Software/SoftwarePurpose/specification", "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition", "The Element is a plan, guideline or strategy how to create, perform or analyze an application.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/FunctionalSafety/EvidenceType/report", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label", "report", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Security/ExploitCatalogVulnAssessmentRelationship", "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note", "An ExploitCatalogVulnAssessmentRelationship describes if a vulnerability is\nlisted in any exploit catalog such as the\nCISA Known Exploited Vulnerabilities (KEV) Catalog <https://www.cisa.gov/known-exploited-vulnerabilities-catalog>.\n\n*Constraints*\n\n- The relationship type shall be set to hasAssessmentFor.\n\n*Example*\n\n{\n  \"type\": \"security_ExploitCatalogVulnAssessmentRelationship\",\n  \"spdxId\": \"urn:spdx.dev:exploit-catalog-1\",\n  \"relationshipType\": \"hasAssessmentFor\",\n  \"security_catalogType\": \"kev\",\n  \"locator\": \"https://www.cisa.gov/known-exploited-vulnerabilities-catalog\",\n  \"security_exploited\": \"true\",\n  \"from\": \"urn:spdx.dev:vuln-cve-2023-2136\",\n  \"to\": [\"urn:product-google-chrome-112.0.5615.136\"],\n  \"suppliedBy\": \"urn:spdx.dev:agent-jane-doe\",\n  \"security_publishedTime\": \"2021-03-09T11:04:53Z\"\n}", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/endTime", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "The point in time when an element or an action ends,\nbecomes no longer applicable, or becomes no longer valid.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
